  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The Dodgers are up four and the A's never led once. That's the whole game right there.",
    "what_this_means": "Springs couldn't get out of the fifth. The Dodgers scored in bunches. Two in the first, three in the third. And by the time the Athletics clawed back two runs in the seventh, LA had already put it away. Colby Thomas hit a solo shot and drove in two, kept them breathing, but breathing wasn't enough. They left three runners on base in scoring position and converted none of them. The bullpen. Alvarado clean for two-thirds, then Hartlieb for three innings. At least didn't compound it, but there was nothing to protect by then. Fifteen strikeouts. Seven hits. That's not an offense, that's attendance.",
    "what_to_watch": "They never made it matter.",
